Description: Headless daemon for Ötzi threshold signing
 otzi-headless is a daemon variant of Ötzi for automated and federated
 custody (bridge reserves, liquidity pools, multi-party server vaults). N
 daemons hold FROST key shares of one key-path-only Taproot key and jointly
 sign Bitcoin spends that every node has checked against its own key and
 its own approval gate.
 .
 The daemon is a signing backend: an authorized operator sends it a
 proposal over its local API and gets the signed transaction back. It has
 no chain access; the caller builds the proposal and broadcasts the result.
 Triggers, chain watching, and decision logic live in operator
 infrastructure.
